resume() derives from the published state without waiting for a writer
still preparing in a head built on the failed write: the version chain
refuses the derivation, and resume() fails with a logic error (#754).
Guarded-by: "resume: waits for a writer still holding a head built on the failed write"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db_degraded.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db_degraded.cpp
index fb989e60..d9da1412 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db_degraded.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db_degraded.cpp
@@ -80,8 +80,6 @@ void DB::resume() {
   // writers are refused at entry while the engine is degraded, so no new
   // holder appears, and each lets go without resume(), write_mu_ or the
   // flush role (see "Holders of the head" in docs/bytecask_design.md).
-  while (current->key_dir.has_successor())
-    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::microseconds{50});
 
   // resume() seals the active file like a rotation does.
   wait_for_hint_backlog();
